  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are positive and \\(a\\ne1,\\) \\(b\\ne1,\\) then the value of \\(b^{\\log_b a}\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "dependent upon \\(b\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "dependent upon \\(a\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "dependent upon \\(a\\) and \\(b\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "zero"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "one"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p28.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By the definition of a logarithm, \\[ b^{\\log_b a}=a. \\] Thus the value depends on \\(a,\\) not on the choice of admissible base \\(b.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the inverse relationship between a base-\\(b\\) logarithm and exponentiation by \\(b\\)",
        "If \\(u=\\log_b a,\\) then \\(b^u=a\\)"
      ],
